{#- The same header on every page: the name on the left, the four places you can be,
    the language, the bell and the account. It is one file because copies of a navigation
    bar drift apart — they had already drifted into three different orders once.

    The order is how often somebody wants each one (design.md §12, "Home is Your targums,
    and Continue leads it", 2026-10-08). Your targums is home: Continue at its top, what
    you started under it. Library is finding the next thing; Your Progress is deliberate
    study; Upload, bringing a text of your own, is the rarest. Learn led the row until
    that day, and was taken apart: its questions for a new reader are `/welcome`, its
    suggestion is on home, and the conversation was already the pill at the foot of
    every page.

    Upload is the one place that keeps its glyph at a desk — a `+` before the word. It
    said Add until 2026-10-08: "Upload" is the less ambiguous word, and the one the
    product uses for what a reader brought ("Uploaded by you").

    Your Progress was called Words until it became an account of what a reader has built
    rather than a list of what they had kept. Two two-word labels are why the row wraps
    rather than scrolls under a narrow window.

    Set `here` to "texts", "library", "progress", "add" or a page's own name before
    including this. -#}
{{ chrome_face() }}
<header class="site-head">
  <div class="site-head-row">
    {#- The lockup, assembled live rather than dropped in as lockup.svg: the name is
        real text in the reading face the page already loads, so it stays selectable and
        scales with the user's type size, and the mark takes its two colours from the
        palette so it turns over with the theme. -#}
    <a class="brand" href="/">
      <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
        <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <span>targum</span>
    </a>
    {%- if here == 'door' %}
    {#- A door in front of the account (an expired link, design.md §12, "The boards are
        the desk"): the bar, and the one place a stranger may go, as board ErrorsDesk
        draws it. No places that would only send them back here, no bell, no account. -#}
    <nav class="site-nav door-nav" aria-label="{{ t("nav.pages", "Pages") }}">
      <a href="/library" data-nav="library">{{ t("nav.library", "Library") }}</a>
    </nav>
    {%- else %}
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="{{ t("nav.pages", "Pages") }}">
      {#- On a phone the four places are a bar at the foot of the window, a glyph over
          each word (phase 4, 2026-09-11); at a desk only Upload draws its glyph. §7: sixteen
          pixels, a stroke at 1.4, round caps. -#}
      <a href="/" data-nav="texts"{% if here == 'texts' %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 13.5h11M3.5 13.5V4h2.5v9.5M7 13.5V2.5h2.5v11M10.8 13.5l-.3-8.2 2.4-.2.3 8.4"/></svg><span class="nav-many"><span class="nav-your">{{ t("nav.your-many", "Your") }} </span>{{ t("nav.targums", "targums") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/library" data-nav="library"{% if here == 'library' %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 2.5h2.5v11H2.5zM6.5 2.5H9v11H6.5zM10.2 3.2l2.4-.6 2.6 10.6-2.4.6z"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.library", "Library") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/progress" data-nav="progress"{% if here == 'progress' %} class="on" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 13.5h11M3.5 11l3-3.5 2.5 2 3.5-4.5"/></svg><span><span class="nav-your">{{ t("nav.your", "Your") }} </span>{{ t("nav.progress", "Progress") }}</span></a>
      <a href="/add" data-nav="add" class="nav-add{% if here == 'add' %} on{% endif %}"{% if here == 'add' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}><svg class="nav-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 3.5v9M3.5 8h9"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.upload", "Upload") }}</span></a>
    </nav>
    {#- Which language (design.md §13, 2026-09-13): one menu at the end of the places on
        every desk page, filled by `lang.js`. Always drawn, with the language's badge,
        for a reader of one language too, since it is also where another is started
        (design.md §12, "The boards are the desk", 2026-10-09). -#}
    {%- if here in ('texts', 'chat', 'library', 'progress', 'add', 'yours', 'you', 'missing', 'subscribe', 'connect', 'press', 'plans') %}
    <div class="langs" id="langs" hidden></div>
    {%- endif %}
    {#- Notifications, in the corner of every page (2026-09-11): what is building and
        what is ready, and anything else the page has to say later. The bell carries a
        count; the panel lists them, newest first, each with its own × and Clear all
        above them; the panel stays open while you put lines away. It replaced the
        pill that stood fixed at the foot of the window. Drawn by `building.js`. -#}
    {#- Search's own door (2026-09-11; one search since 2026-10-09, design.md §12, "One
        search, everywhere"), beside the bell; ⌘K and / are the others. -#}
    <button type="button" class="palette-open" id="palette-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="palette" aria-label="{{ t("nav.search", "Search") }}" data-tip="/" title="{{ t("nav.search-key", "Search (/)") }}">
      <svg class="bell" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4.2"/><path d="M10.2 10.2 13.5 13.5"/></svg>
    </button>
    <div class="notices" id="notices">
      <button type="button" id="notices-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.notifications", "Notifications") }}">
        <svg class="bell" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 2.2a3.6 3.6 0 0 0-3.6 3.6v2.4L3.2 10.6h9.6l-1.2-2.4V5.8A3.6 3.6 0 0 0 8 2.2zM6.6 12.6a1.4 1.4 0 0 0 2.8 0"/></svg>
        <span class="notices-count" id="notices-count" hidden></span>
      </button>
      <div class="notices-panel" id="notices-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.notifications", "Notifications") }}" hidden>
        {#- Clear all (2026-09-14): every line put away at once, as each × would. Shown
            only while there is something to clear. -#}
        <div class="notices-head" id="notices-head" hidden>
          <button type="button" class="btn text small notices-clear" id="notices-clear">{{ t("nav.clear-all", "Clear all") }}</button>
        </div>
        <p class="notices-empty" id="notices-empty">{{ t("nav.we-re-not-building-anything-right-now", "Nothing new.") }}</p>
        <ul class="notices-list" id="notices-list"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="account" id="account">
      <button type="button" id="account-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog">
        {{ t("nav.sign-in", "Sign in") }}
      </button>
      <div class="account-panel" id="account-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="{{ t("nav.your-account", "Your account") }}" hidden>
        {#- What the menu holds (design.md §12, "The account menu is who, what is left, and
            three rows", 2026-10-09): who you are, the month's credits, and three rows with
            the reader menus' anatomy. Your words and phrases, Your subscriptions and Your
            playlists stood here as bold links until that day; they are reached from Your
            Progress and from the tabs of Your targums, and three copies of the navigation
            in a corner is clutter. -#}
        {#- On a phone the top bar keeps the mark, the language, the bell and the account
            (design.md §13), so find is here (2026-09-14). -#}
        <p class="account-phone">
          <button type="button" class="btn tonal small account-find" data-palette-open>{{ t("nav.search", "Search") }}</button>
        </p>
        <div class="signed-out">
          <p>{{ t("nav.your-words-follow-you-no-password-we", "Your words follow you. No password. We'll email you a link.") }}</p>
          <form id="account-form">
            <input type="email" class="well" id="account-email" placeholder="{{ t("nav.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}"
                   autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" required>
            <button type="submit" class="btn filled small">{{ t("nav.send-a-link", "Send a link") }}</button>
          </form>
          {#- Saved on this device belongs to the browser, not the account, so it is a row
              whether or not anybody is signed in. -#}
          <div class="menu-rows">
            <a class="menu-row" href="/you/saved">{{ t("nav.saved-on-this-device", "Saved on this device") }}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="signed-in" hidden>
          <div class="account-head">
            <p class="whom" id="account-whom"></p>
            {#- The month's credits, where a reader who wonders looks, and nowhere they did
                not (targum-internal#237): what is left and when it comes back, with the
                rate under it, because a balance always carries its rate (§12, "A cost is
                credits", 2026-09-23). -#}
            <p class="hours" id="account-hours" hidden></p>
            <p class="rate" id="account-rate" hidden></p>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-rows">
            <a class="menu-row" href="/you">{{ t("nav.your-account", "Your account") }}</a>
            <a class="menu-row" href="/you/saved">{{ t("nav.saved-on-this-device", "Saved on this device") }}</a>
            <button type="button" class="menu-row" id="account-out">{{ t("nav.sign-out", "Sign out") }}</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="said" id="account-said" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>
{#- The page's title stands on the desk under the bar, in the reading serif at 34px, and
    never inside the bar (design.md §12, "The boards are the desk", 2026-10-09): every
    desk page the same, in the one column the bar's row and the foot stand in. Where a
    page stands inside a place is said above it: the Tanakh map is Library › Tanakh.
    `crumbs` is a list of (name, address). -#}
{%- if title or crumbs or here in ('texts', 'library', 'progress') %}
<div class="page-head">
  {%- if crumbs %}
  <nav class="site-crumbs" aria-label="{{ t("nav.where-you-are", "Where you are") }}">
    {%- for name, address in crumbs %}<a href="{{ address }}">{{ name }}</a><span class="crumb-step" aria-hidden="true"> › </span>{% endfor %}<span aria-current="page">{{ title }}</span>
  </nav>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if title %}
  <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}{% if title_he %} <bdi class="page-title-he" lang="he" dir="rtl">{{ title_he }}</bdi>{% endif %}</h1>
  {%- endif %}
  {#- What stands at the far end of the title's row, where a board puts it: the Tanakh's
      Map and List of books (board LibraryTanakh). A template's name. -#}
  {%- if title_aside %}
  <div class="page-head-aside">{% include title_aside %}</div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if here in ('texts', 'library', 'progress') %}
  <p class="beta-note" id="beta-note" hidden></p>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- if here != 'door' %}
{#- What a reader follows, on every page (2026-09-11): the bell says when a followed
    series' instalment lands, and home puts it first under Continue. Before `building.js`, which
    every page includes after this header and which asks it. -#}
<script>{{ asset('follow.js') }}</script>
{%- endif %}
{#- How a refusal is drawn (design.md §12, 2026-10-09): under a field, a line, a panel,
    and the connection's banner, which `fault.js` puts at the foot of this header. -#}
<script>{{ asset('fault.js') }}</script>
{%- if here != 'door' %}
{#- Talk to targum, from anywhere (2026-09-11): one pill fixed at the foot of every page
    opens the conversation as a drawer — the conversation page framed without its bar.
    Nothing is loaded until it is opened. Drawn by `talk.js`. -#}
<button type="button" class="talk-cta" id="talk-open" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="talk-drawer" aria-label="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}"><svg class="talk-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 2.5c-3.3 0-6 2.2-6 5 0 1.5.8 2.9 2.1 3.8L3.5 13.5l3-1.3c.5.1 1 .2 1.5.2 3.3 0 6-2.2 6-5s-2.7-4.9-6-4.9z"/></svg><span>{{ t("nav.talk", "Talk") }}</span></button>
<div class="scrim talk-scrim" id="talk-scrim" hidden></div>
{#- Drawn as boards ChatDesk and ChatPhone (design.md §12, "Talk is a sheet over a dimmed
    page", 2026-10-09): the shared `.scrim` under it at every width, the title in the
    reading serif, and on a phone the shared `.sheet-grab`, which closes it. -#}
<aside class="talk-drawer" id="talk-drawer" aria-label="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}" hidden>
  <button type="button" class="sheet-grab talk-grab" data-talk-close aria-label="{{ t("nav.close", "Close") }}"></button>
  <div class="talk-drawer-head">
    <div class="talk-drawer-names">
      <span class="talk-drawer-title">{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}</span>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="talk-close" id="talk-close" aria-label="{{ t("nav.close", "Close") }}"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 4l8 8M12 4l-8 8"/></svg></button>
  </div>
  <iframe class="talk-frame" id="talk-frame" title="{{ t("nav.talk-to-targum", "Talk to targum") }}" allow="microphone" data-src="/chat?embed=1{% if token %}&amp;k={{ token }}{% endif %}"></iframe>
</aside>
<script>{{ asset('talk.js') }}</script>
{#- One search, everywhere (design.md §12, "One search, everywhere", 2026-10-09): the
    bar's door, ⌘K and / open it, and the Library's own box opens it held to the Library.
    The field, the language it searches in, the filters, and what it found, grouped.
    Drawn by `palette.js`, from `/search.json`. Every row's picture is `covers.js`'s,
    which every page with this bar carries from here. -#}
<script>{{ asset('covers.js') }}</script>
<div class="scrim palette-scrim" id="palette-scrim" hidden></div>
<div class="palette" id="palette" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="{{ t("nav.search-targum", "Search targum") }}" hidden>
  <div class="palette-top">
    <button type="button" class="palette-back" id="palette-back" aria-label="{{ t("nav.close", "Close") }}"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 3.5 5.5 8l4.5 4.5"/></svg></button>
    <label class="palette-field">
      <svg class="palette-lens" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4.2"/><path d="M10.2 10.2 13.5 13.5"/></svg>
      <input type="search" id="palette-find" class="palette-find" dir="auto" placeholder="{{ t("nav.search-placeholder", "Titles, authors, topics or a word") }}" aria-label="{{ t("nav.search-targum", "Search targum") }}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" enterkeyhint="search">
      <button type="button" class="palette-clear" id="palette-clear" aria-label="{{ t("nav.clear-search", "Clear the search") }}" hidden>×</button>
      <kbd class="palette-esc">Esc</kbd>
    </label>
    <div class="palette-scope">
      <button type="button" class="palette-lang" id="palette-lang" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="palette-langs"></button>
      <div class="palette-langs" id="palette-langs" role="menu" hidden></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="tabs palette-filters" id="palette-filters" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ t("nav.search-where", "Where to look") }}"></div>
  <div class="palette-body" id="palette-body" aria-live="polite"></div>
</div>
<script>{{ asset('palette.js') }}</script>
{#- Saving for offline, and the worker that answers what was saved when the network is
    not there (design.md §12, 2026-10-09). -#}
<script>{{ asset('offline.js') }}</script>
{%- endif %}
